{"id": "EUVD-2026-103876", "enisaUuid": "afffda87-18e3-376a-b49c-40f9b005610d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/mlx5e: Fix AF_XDP TX timestamp teardown NULL dereference\n\nDuring XSK TX queue teardown, outstanding descriptors are completed\nwithout a CQE. If one requested a TX timestamp, the completion path\npasses that NULL CQE to mlx5e_xsk_fill_timestamp(), which dereferences\nit.\n\nReturn zero when no CQE is available, indicating that teardown did not\nproduce a TX timestamp.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:25:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fce70b6bf9f3261e887419a4e7caa25b80fa9d55", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f81d40e2eb69552334f510114f3e6edd0d43178b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/63df0ef4c6e3105589e6bb2e758ce611b0ada86c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7b97273cbebe9dd4fddc457f0c4f2a124d0e3996"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5f42-c4x2-rx63", "CVE-2026-98791"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02f6c178-d5ef-332f-b08d-b6527547753d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec706a860eba99bf934d59f74b5db90af44e882e <63df0ef4c6e3105589e6bb2e758ce611b0ada86c"}, {"id": "055719e4-8b45-3117-b2a9-20781d53242f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec706a860eba99bf934d59f74b5db90af44e882e <7b97273cbebe9dd4fddc457f0c4f2a124d0e3996"}, {"id": "0b5543d8-4f93-3f09-9bf9-08bb7e008707", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "15da01f3-7f7c-33d9-91f0-8dcd92f09e08", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a868e100-2309-39e6-9705-b84ca62d11f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec706a860eba99bf934d59f74b5db90af44e882e <fce70b6bf9f3261e887419a4e7caa25b80fa9d55"}, {"id": "b63963c0